; Stage 15 W3c fallout: an unnamed `declare` parameter is a TYPE operand, so a
; spelling that names no type is a located error. Silently defaulting it to `i32`
; is precisely what hid the original defect, so there is nothing to fall back to.
(declare w3d_unknown (i64 NoSuchDeclParamType):void)

(defn main ():i32 (return 0))
